ote":"aye"},{"name":"Jordon Steele-John","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10901","person_slug":"jordon-steele-john","vote":"no"},{"name":"Josh Dolega","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11054","person_slug":"josh-dolega","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Karen Grogan","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10965","person_slug":"karen-grogan","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Katy Gallagher","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10838","person_slug":"katy-gallagher","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Larissa Waters","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10764","person_slug":"larissa-waters","vote":"no"},{"name":"Lidia Thorpe","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10961","person_slug":"lidia-thorpe","vote":"no"},{"name":"Lisa Darmanin","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11021","person_slug":"lisa-darmanin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Marielle Smith","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10953","person_slug":"marielle-smith","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Mehreen Faruqi","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10912","person_slug":"mehreen-faruqi","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michelle Ananda-Rajah","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10983","person_slug":"michelle-ananda-rajah","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Murray Watt","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10857","person_slug":"murray-watt","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Nick McKim","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10841","person_slug":"nick-mckim","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nita Green","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10950","person_slug":"nita-green","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Paul Scarr","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10949","person_slug":"paul-scarr","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Penny Allman-Payne","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11002","person_slug":"penny-allman-payne","vote":"no"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Dowling","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11056","person_slug":"richard-dowling","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Motions — Middle East","noes":13,"question":"David Shoebridge I seek leave to move a motion relating to the proposed Australian military deployment to the Middle East as circulated. Leave not granted. Pursuant to contingent notice, standing in the name of Senator Waters, I move: That so much of the standing orders be suspended as would prevent me from moving a motion to provide for the consideration of the matter, namely a motion to give precedence to a motion relating to the proposed Australian military deployment to the Middle East. The motion that the Greens are bringing to this house—no doubt, it will be opposed by the three war parties: Labor, the coalition and One Nation—is: That the Senate: (a) notes that the Australian public rejects Labor's push to be part of another US-led forever war in the Middle East, which has already seen thousands of civilians injured and killed and the world spiralling into economic chaos and even greater insecurity; and (b) calls on the Government to immediately end support for the US and Israeli war with Iran, withdraw all Australian troops from the US military, prohibit the US from using Australian-based military assets, and not send any Australian troops to the region to participate in this illegal war. I know that there will be resistance to this. The government say that they desperately think that they should get onto the 'Transitional amendments No. 4 Defence veterans bill' or that some other thing is more urgent than this motion, but I can tell you now that the Australian public are watching in horror as Labor drags them into another US forever war. Labor is doing it with the support from the other two war parties in here—the coalition and One Nation. Between you, you've never seen a US war you didn't want to back in. You've never seen a demand from Donald Trump that you haven't wanted to bend over to grant—whenever he asks! If it's 2 am in the morning—whenever he asks! We have, today, in just one week, seen how this war has escalated—the economic chaos and the killing","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10028","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-03-10/6"}
